    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0266" n="1316" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower
                    Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman file,
                        Dulles–Herter series</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President
                        to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-03-25">March 25, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had hoped to talk to you this morning about the Kashmir situation. If you
                    believe that Paul Hoffman could do some
                    good by going on a private mission I think we should, by all means, send him at
                    once. Our world simply cannot afford an outbreak of hostilities between these
                    two countries, and I would risk a great deal to prevent any such
                    eventuality.</p>
                <closer><signed>D[<hi rendition="#small-caps">wight</hi>]
                            D. E[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >isenhower</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
